      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #66, Bugs27 #48 residual,
      ⍝ 2026-08-11): a rank mismatch in A,[X]B (laminate) raised INDEX
      ⍝ ERROR instead of RANK ERROR, even though the )MORE text itself
      ⍝ already says "expecting ⍴⍴A = ⍴⍴B"; and laminate's own Z, when B
      ⍝ is empty, always took its prototype from B instead of A (rank>=2),
      ⍝ unlike plain catenate which already got this right for #48.
      ⍝
      Z←1 2 3,[0.5]2 3⍴0
RANK ERROR+
      Z←1 2 3,[0.5]2 3⍴0
        ^    ^
      )MORE
A,[X]B: expecting ⍴⍴A = ⍴⍴B (or A or B a scalar); ⍴⍴A is 1, ⍴⍴B is 2

      ⎕UCS ↑(0 3⍴'a'),[0.5]0 3⍴0
